<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41431" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί-τριπτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
		of persons to whom one says <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιτριβείης</span> (= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄξιος τοῦ
			ἐπιτριβῆναι,</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			<u>EM</u>
			367.1
		</span></i>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>accursed, damned,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὐπίτριπτον κίναδος</span> the
				<i>damned</i> fox, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				103
			</span></i> (= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἐξῶλες θηρίον,</span>
			Sch.), cf.<i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.99
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ψωμοκόλακες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sannyr.
					10
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὑπίτριπτος</span> the
				<i>rogue,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				275
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
				105
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				619
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦπίτριπτε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ach.</u>
					557
				</span></i>
			 ; <i>rascally,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥήτορες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Tim.</u>
					37
				</span></i>
			 : 
				Sup.
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Com.Adesp.</u>
				1348
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ νῦν ἐ. καὶ κατεαγυῖα μουσική</span>
			the <i>disreputable</i> and effeminate music of to-day, <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				6.14
			</span></i>. (For this sense of a participial formation, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐλόμενος</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀνήμενος.</span>)</div>
